<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Ras al-Khaimah</h1><p class="st-meta">1708 CE – 1972 CE (approx.) · capital Ras al-Khaimah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The seat of the Qawasim, a seafaring dynasty whose fleets challenged the British in the Gulf and who joined the UAE in 1972.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Qawasim</a>, an Arab tribe on the northern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> peninsula, established themselves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a>, near the old port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julfar">Julfar</a>, in the early 18th century. They built a maritime power with branches on both shores of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Gulf</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandar-lengeh">Lingeh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sharjah</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Qawasim</a> lived from pearling, trade and sea warfare. Their attacks on shipping, partly linked to alliance with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-diriyah">Emirate of Diriyah</a>, led the British to call the area the Pirate Coast. British expeditions in 1809 and 1819 destroyed their fleet and town, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a> made the sheikhdom one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>. It was ruled with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sharjah</a> at times and separated permanently in 1921.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> stayed out of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> at its founding in 1971, hoping for oil and a dispute over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-and-lesser-tunbs">Tunb islands</a>, seized by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. It joined in February 1972 under Sheikh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saqr-bin-mohammed-al-qasimi">Saqr bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Ras al-Khaimah" width="320" height="180"><figcaption>Image: Stevenmccombe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_RAK_City_from_Al_Qawasim_Corniche_flagpole.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1708 CE – 1972 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ras al-Khaimah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sultan bin Saqr Al Qasimi, Saqr bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ras al-Khaimah, Emirate of Ras al-Khaimah, Qawasim</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Ras al-Khaimah on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6164 1226 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Ras al-Khaimah lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6484 1482L6237 1523M6484 1482L4997 651M6484 1482L6439 1557M6484 1482L6468 1502M6484 1482L6446 1533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6237 1523h0M4997 651h0M6439 1557h0M6468 1502h0M6446 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6484 1482h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6484 1482h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
